From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: share identical next hops

Every flow currently allocates a private next hop, even when hundreds
of flows use the same gateway or wireless station. IPQ5332 has only
768 next-hop rows; a multi-connection download fills this table long
before exhausting the 2048 flow entries and repeatedly fails offload.

Cache immutable next hops by all hardware rewrite fields: egress port,
L3 interface, destination MAC, both VLAN tags, public NAT index and
DNAT address. Compare the fields explicitly to avoid struct padding.
Acquire a reference before publishing each flow and release it only
after confirmed hardware deletion or pre-publication rollback.
Quarantined flows retain their references and cannot lose their row
when another sharing flow is removed. Purge remaining cache objects
at driver teardown. Report occupied rows and references in debugfs.

The per-flow NAT port, MTU, source-interface check, PPPoE/VLAN lifetime
and packet counters remain independent. True resource exhaustion still
fails open through the existing software path.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
